  "input_edits": {
    "exporter": "Use the original KeyValueStore.tla. To MCKVS append the two cleanup/conflict predicates, then SomeCommit and FullHasFresh as listed below. From MCKVSSafetyLarge.cfg, replace Key, Val and TxId with the requested k1..kK, v1..vV and t1..tT model values. Add INVARIANT SomeCommit and INVARIANT FullHasFresh after the original invariants. Remove only SYMMETRY TxIdSymmetric for labeled rows, keeping the TxIdSymmetric definition in the source. The no-unused controls also remove that single now-dead definition.",
    "predicates": "TxIsClean == \\A t \\in TxId \\ tx : missed[t] = {}\nAtMostOneConflict == \\A a \\in tx : \\A b \\in tx :\n    a /= b => ((missed[a] \\cap written[a]) = {} \\/ (missed[b] \\cap written[b]) = {})\nSomeCommit == tx = TxId => \\E t \\in tx : (missed[t] \\cap written[t]) = {}\nFullHasFresh == tx = TxId => \\E t \\in tx : missed[t] = {}",
    "complete_search": "Use original MCKVS.tla on 2 keys, 2 values and 3 transactions with the original transaction symmetry and both original invariants. Wrap with Library.tla below and add CONSTANT Peer = {p1, ..., p12} to its CFG. The small control uses only {p1,p2}. The twelve-peer group is never configured nor referenced.",
    "Library.tla": "---- MODULE Library ----\nEXTENDS MCKVS\nCONSTANT Peer\nUnused == Permutations(Peer)\n====\n",
    "startup_controls": "Probe uses x=0, a transition alternating 0 and 1, layout invariant x in {0,1}, an unused pure Permutations(Id), used Needed == Cardinality(Id), ASSUME Needed > 0 and two IDs. Good checks Needed=2 and x in {0,1}; Bad checks x=0. The assume control changes the assumption to Needed=0. The print control replaces the unused permutation with PrintT(\"notice\"). sym-limit selects the actual seven-ID permutation group."
  },
